{
  "$schema": "../../schema/incident.schema.json",
  "protocol": "Biswap",
  "name": "Biswap V3Migrator migrate() burns any approver's V2 LP with unchecked pair and tokens",
  "summary": "V3Migrator.migrate(params) pulls params.liquidityToMigrate of params.pair LP from params.recipient rather than from the caller, burns it into the migrator, mints a V3 position in params.token0/params.token1 for the recipient and refunds the unused amounts to the recipient, without checking that the tokens are the pair's or that the pair is genuine. Anyone could thus spend the LP of every holder who had approved the migrator. In the anchor the attacker's contract first migrated victim 0x1bc2bb87's 2,187.77 BSW/WBNB LP with two fake tokens, leaving the real 121,855.90 BSW and 51.32 WBNB in the migrator and giving the victim a fake-token position, then called migrate with itself as the 'pair' (its burn() reporting those balances) and BSW/WBNB as the tokens, receiving a V3 position holding the BSW and the WBNB as refund. Three attackers and four smaller copycats repeated it in 85 more transactions over the next 12 weeks (last at block 31919657).",
