  "notes": [
    "Target is the V3Migrator, created at block 29525530 by 0x321fb100 a day before the anchor; resets.mjs finds no later change. The victims' approvals are their own state and not a reset.",
    "Earlier exploits: all 626 transactions with a migrator event from its creation to block 32200000 were checked for LP that a party other than the transaction's sender or target sent to its pair for burning. The first is the anchor (0x1bc2bb87's LP, block 29552670); every earlier migration burned the sender's own LP. 86 transactions qualify, matching campaign.mjs's 86 exercises (it found three whose logs the BSC node attributes to neighbouring transactions): by 0xa1e31b29 (30), 0xa7a98876 (22, including the DeFiHackLabs transaction 0xebe52488), 0xe3aeede5 (17, among them the USDT/BUSD LP of 0xa68cc3d7 and 0x7f46134c, worth 332k and 362k) and four senders working through 0x73f3c0df (17 transactions, 103,332 USD, mostly 0x639ce846's 228 WBNB and 50,000 BUSD).",
    "Loss is the underlying of the burned third-party LP (the pair's transfers to the migrator in those 83 transactions), priced per transaction at DefiLlama (coingecko keys for USDT, BUSD, ETH, SHIB, SAND, NEAR and USDC, whose BSC keys return nothing). It is far above the 72k in DeFiHackLabs and DefiLlama, which cover only part of the first attackers' take; the V3 positions in fake tokens the victims received are worthless and not subtracted."
  ]
}
